encyclopedia :resonance do
  name "Resonance"
  summary "Resonance is an ambient energy throughout the Kaleidos system that tuned ringglass channels into structural, kinetic, and signal effects."
  kind :phenomenon
  subkind :physical_system
  status :complete
  reviewed "2026-06-18"
  topics :resonance
  prevalence :common
  available_globally
  registry true
  function "Carries power, motion and information through tuned materials"
  nature "Ambient energy present throughout the Kaleidos system"
  known_forms "Structural, kinetic and signal bands"
  operating_limit "Local fields deplete and effects fade away from ringglass"

  prose <<~PROSE
    Resonance is an ambient energy measured throughout the Kaleidos system. Its strength varies across Kaleidos, the moons, the #{ref :the_glass_frontier, "ring habs"}, and the outer bodies. Ringglass concentrates and channels the field in stable frequencies, allowing a tuned piece to reinforce matter, transmit force, or carry information.

    The ring's builders joined tuned sections of #{encyclopedia_ref :ringglass, "ringglass"} into continuous systems. Energy, data, and physical force passed from one section to the next as a conducted vibration. The ring's structures, transit, and communications all depended on those linked arrays.

    The #{ref :the_glassfall, "Glassfall"} scattered those arrays through orbit and across Kaleidos's soil and water. Trillions of fragments now strengthen the local field wherever debris has settled. After #{elapsed :the_glassfall, approx: true}, most inhabited ground contains enough crystal for broad household devices, while professional work relies on cut ringglass and denser arrays.

    Present practice reproduces broad and mid-band effects with cruder instruments than the #{encyclopedia_ref :elves, "elves"} used. Surviving artifacts establish narrower effects that current workshops can measure but seldom reproduce.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :how_it_works, heading: "How It Works"
    Practitioners describe resonance by **band**, which names the physical effect, and **bandwidth**, which describes how tightly the application is focused.

    ### The Three Known Bands

    Tuned ringglass produces three established bands:

    **Structural** resonance reinforces physical bonds. It makes materials harder, denser, and more resilient; ringglass-reinforced concrete is standard construction on Kaleidos.

    **Kinetic** resonance produces motion, heat, and force. It powers #{encyclopedia_ref :kite, "kites"}, refineries, and generators. Kinetic-tuned ringglass redirects opposing forces into a frequency null space, allowing thrust with greatly reduced resistance.

    **Signal** resonance carries information for communication, storage, and navigation. Loose signal-tuned crystal can retain and retransmit encountered data; the #{encyclopedia_ref :echo_rivers, "Echo Rivers"} carry pre-Glassfall transmissions through crystal-bearing water. Controlled arrays carry live messages and allow the #{ref :echo_ledger_conclave, "Echo Ledger Conclave"} to recover old records from ambient traffic.

    ### Bandwidth

    Bandwidth varies continuously, but workshops and surveys use three working ranges:

    **Broad bandwidth** uses a wide range of frequencies and tolerates low-grade ringglass. Lanterns, stoves, compasses, and basic heaters operate here. A broad structural application strengthens a wall; a broad kinetic application heats a room.

    **Mid bandwidth** requires quality arrays or trained #{encyclopedia_ref :resonant_tuner, "Tuners"}. Kite drives, refineries, long-range communication, and #{ref :clarisant, "Clarisant"}-grade attunement work use this range. Mid kinetic arrays generate sustained thrust, while mid signal arrays carry speech across a continent.

    **Narrow bandwidth** concentrates the field tightly enough to produce effects outside ordinary workshop practice. Structural examples alter local physical behavior, kinetic examples produce translocation, and signal examples transfer information directly into consciousness.

    #{ref :bloom_zones, "Bloom Zone"} relics, pre-Glassfall artifacts, and deep #{ref :the_shear, "Shear"} anomalies exhibit narrow-band characteristics. The custodians of the #{ref :lattice_proxy_synod, "Lattice Proxy Synod"} appear to process information in narrow signal frequencies, which makes their communication difficult to receive or answer with contemporary equipment.

    Spell registries use the tier names **broad**, **focused**, and **narrow**. *Focused* is the registry term for a spell worked in the middle bandwidth. Each spell is registered once, at the narrowest bandwidth its effect requires; casting it with more force does not move it to another tier. Mantles enlarge or transform particular spells without adding another bandwidth category. Single-wavelength resonance remains a proposed limit beyond the registered tiers.

    Clarisant registries usually give a reproducible spell one short work-word whose technical meaning comes from the casting: #{encyclopedia_ref :step, "Step"}, #{encyclopedia_ref :echoing, "Echoing"}, #{encyclopedia_ref :mending, "Mending"}, #{encyclopedia_ref :seaming, "Seaming"}, #{encyclopedia_ref :stay, "Stay"}, and #{encyclopedia_ref :unclosing, "Unclosing"}. Workings kept by a particular trade retain service names such as #{encyclopedia_ref :signal_folding, "Signal Folding"} and #{encyclopedia_ref :crucible_veiling, "Crucible Veiling"}; Tessellan-derived spells retain the language of Form and Will. A registry name belongs to one reproducible casting, not to every stronger act that resembles it.

    Manufactured devices enclose their tuning, so an operator can use a mid-band array without tuning it. Tuners set and maintain those frequencies deliberately. Narrow-band work remains confined to relic study, controlled surveys, and accidental exposures.

    **Single-wavelength resonance** is the proposed limit beyond narrow bandwidth: one exact frequency with no measured spread or interference. Pre-Glassfall artifacts attributed to this practice transfer energy with near-zero measured waste, cross established band boundaries, or carry signals across gaps in the conductive medium. Contemporary laboratories have documented those behaviors but have not produced an equivalent field. The surviving measurements define the theory; reports that the elves were developing it before the Glassfall remain unverified.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :significance, heading: "The Geometry of Coherence"
    The band-and-bandwidth model guides workshop practice. #{encyclopedia_ref :the_three_forms, "The Three Forms"} describes the same observations through geometry: a coherent vibration closes into a stable figure, structural and kinetic resonance close toward different figures, and signal follows the path between them. It calls perfect coherence the One Truth.

    Engineering tables do not use the cosmology's figures as frequencies, but tuners still use closure to describe a stable response. In ringglass, incomplete closure appears as bleed into adjacent frequencies; a cleanly closed working holds its band under load. That measured correspondence keeps the older language in tuner instruction and ceremony.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :sources, heading: "Ringglass"
    Practical resonance work requires a medium that concentrates the ambient field, carries it, and holds a frequency. #{encyclopedia_ref :ringglass, "Ringglass"} combines those properties at usable strength and occurs throughout the system as debris, sediment, and salvage. Certain mineral formations, crystal-bearing deep water, and several rare alloys conduct more weakly or across fewer frequencies. See the #{encyclopedia_ref :ringglass, "ringglass entry"} for sourcing, grades, processing, and trade.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :applications, heading: "Ambient Field"
    Kaleidos and the inhabited ring contain enough ringglass in soil, rock, building materials, and dust to sustain a usable local field in most settlements. Broad-band lanterns, stoves, heaters, compasses, and basic communicators draw from that field through their own tuned pieces.

    Resonance concentrators gather the ambient field through large ringglass arrays and maintain a denser working field around a settlement. Household devices respond more strongly there, and mid-band applications hold their tuning more reliably.

    Heavy use produces #{encyclopedia_ref :drawdown, "drawdown"}: the local ringglass quiets until the field replenishes. Small settlements stagger major work by custom. Larger cities allocate industrial draws under #{ref :tempered_accord, "Tempered Accord"} frameworks and publish protected hours for domestic supply.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :limits, heading: "Limits"
    Each local field supplies a finite rate of work. Heavy draw quiets its ringglass until the field replenishes, over hours in rich connected ground or weeks in sparse geology.

    Resonance conducts through crystal, crystal-laced rock, and water carrying crystal particulate. Its effect falls rapidly across open air or other gaps, so every practical device contains ringglass and long systems require a connected path.

    A tuned piece responds within one frequency range. Structural pieces reinforce, kinetic pieces produce force or heat, and signal pieces carry information. Retuning requires specialized equipment, and repeated changes damage the crystal; most devices use purpose-cut pieces for one function.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :limits, heading: "Feeling It Work"
    Species with an innate sense for resonance — #{encyclopedia_ref :gnomes, "gnomes"} above all — perceive active fields directly in species-specific ways. Other bystanders generally require an instrument to detect low-power signal work.

    Heavy structural or kinetic draws produce a bodily pressure across species: teeth and joints seem to align toward the active lattice, and balance shifts toward it. The sensation identifies nearby high-power work before an instrument reading and intensifies when an array bleeds across frequencies.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :trade, heading: "Who Controls It"
    Access to resonance work depends on refined ringglass, trained tuners, and local allocation. See #{encyclopedia_ref :ringglass, "Ringglass"} for the material's supply and trade.
  PROSE

  cue "Inside most settlements the ambient field already feeds lamps, stoves, heaters, and door compasses through the tuned ringglass in each device. The same devices fade and stop on crystal-poor ground."
  cue "Heavy structural or kinetic work presses at teeth, joints, and balance, drawing the body toward the active lattice before any instrument registers the load."
  affordance "Run something hard — a drive held at full field, a heater through a long night, an array pushed past its usual duty — and the local field goes quiet afterward. Crystal-rich ground recovers in hours; thin rock can take weeks, and everything else drawing on that field waits with them."
  pressure "A tuned piece serves one frequency range, so changing a device's function requires tuner equipment and risks damaging the crystal with each retuning."
  variation "Structural — reinforces physical bonds."
  variation "Kinetic — converts resonance into motion, heat, and force."
  variation "Signal — carries information for communication, storage, and navigation."

end
